  "result": "The last owner can no longer be removed. The fix is in `removeMember` in `src/server/services/member-service.ts`. I haven't run the test suite or added a test for this case.\n\n`removeMember` was calling `assertLastOwnerRetained(orgId, memberId, \"owner\")`. That function returns immediately when the next role is `\"owner\"`, so on removal it never counted the remaining owners. Demotion passed the real target role, which is why it was still refused.\n\n`removeMember` now passes `\"viewer\"` instead, so removal goes through the same owner-count check as a demotion. I kept the function's `Role` signature because the manifest in `scripts/manifest-parts/server.ts` declares it. The catch is that `\"viewer\"` stands in for \"no role\", and a comment at the call site says so.\n\nI also read the owner-counting query, since a bad count would break the check too. It only counts live, non-archived owners, and the check filters out the member being changed, so it behaves correctly.",
